  "scientific_status": "Three explicit experimental-learnability interfaces: (A) convex finitely presented bounded-curvature potential family, positive native bounded gradient error and finite-horizon tasks: compute infimum worst-case accuracy Omega(2delta)/2 with near-optimal finite programme and indistinguishable compatible models, via proved/paid THG/Euler/CAD composition not general executed solver. (B) nonconvex two-programme-presented quadratic prior with uniformly polynomial-bit-time forward evaluators: fixed-margin accuracy-value uncomputability and no computable uniform work bound on learnable instances under specified closed fixed-point channel. (C) executed exact finite-catalogue/budget minimax equilibrium design for whole scalar law family; finite adaptation advantage, separate proved continuum floor. No generic efficient inference, new physical acquisition, PvsNP or civilisation-scale result.",
